            <div class="row">
               <div class="col-12 mb-3">
                  <h1>Howard College Athletics Earns NJCAA Academic Honors</h1>
                  <h2 class="title-decorative font-size-sm">
                     									July 30, 2026
                     								</h2>
               </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row">
               <div class="col-lg-7 col-xl-8">
                  <div class="figure">
                     <div class="figure"><img src="/_resources/images/news/njcaa-academic-teams-of-the-year.png" class="figure-img" alt="NJCAA Academic Teams of the Year  HC Softball - 3.76 Team GPA  HC Women's basketball - 3.74 Team GPA HC Baseball - 3.60 Team GPA  HC Men's basketball - 3.36 Team GPA"><p class="figure-caption">NJCAA Academic Teams of the Year 
                           HC Softball - 3.76 Team GPA 
                           HC Women's basketball - 3.74 Team GPA
                           HC Baseball - 3.60 Team GPA 
                           HC Men's basketball - 3.36 Team GPA</p>
                     </div>
                  </div>
               </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row mt-3">
               <div class="col-12">
                  <div class="post-content mb-5">
                     <h2><strong>Howard College Athletics Earns NJCAA Academic Honors</strong></h2>
                     
                     <p>Howard College is proud to celebrate another outstanding achievement by its student-athletes
                        as the National Junior College Athletic Association (NJCAA) recently announced its
                        2025-26 Academic Team Awards and All-Academic Teams. From team success in the classroom
                        to individual academic excellence, Howard College student-athletes continue to demonstrate
                        that they are committed to achieving at the highest level, both in competition and
                        in the classroom.</p>
                     
                     <p>The NJCAA Academic Team Awards recognize programs that achieve a cumulative team grade
                        point average (GPA) of 3.0 or higher during the academic year. This year, four Howard
                        College athletic programs earned national recognition. In addition to the team honors,
                        student-athletes from every Howard College athletic program were recognized individually
                        by the NJCAA as First Team, Second Team, and Third Team All-Academic honorees.</p>
                     
                     <h3><strong>Howard College Softball ranked 12th in the nation with a 3.76 Team GPA</strong></h3>
                     
                     <p>First team honors were awarded to Sarah Aguilar, Janelle Armadillo, Angelina Corral,
                        Isabella Farinha, Gabriella Gonzales, Eva O’Loughlan, and Bianca Rijborz. Second team
                        honors were awarded to Celeste Flores, Ellie Kissinger, Brynn Rodgers, Sophia Sanches,
                        Cloe Viasana, and Savannah Villarreal. Third team honors were awarded to Aryah Barrera,
                        Annalise Barron, Brooke Carriker, and Sealee Lindley.</p>
                     
                     <h3><strong>Howard College Women's Basketball ranked 6th in the nation with a 3.74 Team GPA</strong></h3>
                     
                     <p>First team honors were awarded to Kailyn Berry and Abrianna Lawrence. Second team
                        honors were awarded to Ella Campbell, Vincinique Dames, Tasiana Butler, Agathe Lerat,
                        and Shannon Quigley. Third team honors were awarded to Makayla Ellison and Talia Vea.</p>
                     
                     <h3><strong>Howard College Baseball ranked 16th in the nation with a 3.60 Team GPA</strong></h3>
                     
                     <p>First team honors were awarded to Reid Brezina, Samuel Distel, Zachary Foden, Adam
                        Hawrylak, Colton Klapprodt, Andrew Lind, Stephen Peterson, Connel Reed, and Jaxon
                        Wylie. Second team honors were awarded to Austin Frye and Lincoln Schroeder. Third
                        team honors were awarded to Jackson Arnett, Cash Bolgiano, Gaston Galvan, Ehtan Guzman,
                        Charles Lavigne, Caiden Perardi, Davis Rodgers, and Owen Skinner.</p>
                     
                     <h3><strong>Howard College Men's Basketball ranked 19th in the nation with a 3.36 Team GPA</strong></h3>
                     
                     <p>First team honors were awarded to Jermaine Cunningham and Florian Rijkers. Second
                        team honors were awarded to Roee Oselka and Oskar Stumer. Third team honors were awarded
                        to Terry Copeland and Kuai Deng.</p>
                     
                     <p>These impressive GPAs reflect the dedication, discipline, and perseverance of Howard
                        College's student-athletes, as well as the support provided by coaches, faculty, and
                        academic staff who help them succeed both on the field and in the classroom.</p>
                     
                     <p>“We are incredibly proud of these teams and athletes,” said Athletic Director Kyle
                        Cooper. “One of the things I appreciate most about this group is their willingness
                        to invest in their future. They show up, put in the work, support one another, and
                        take pride in representing Howard College. That’s the kind of culture we’re committed
                        to building.”</p>
                     
                     <p>The recognition comes on the heels of another remarkable year for Howard College Athletics,
                        including national success. While championships and victories are great accomplishments,
                        the continued academic success of Howard College's athletic programs reinforces the
                        college’s commitment to developing well-rounded students prepared for success long
                        after graduation.</p>
                     
                     <p>Howard College congratulates every student-athlete, coach, and staff member who contributed
                        to these outstanding academic achievements. Their dedication represents the very best
                        of what it means to be a Howard Hawk.</p>
                  </div>
               </div>
            </div>
         </div>
